mfd: rk8xx: keep the sleep pin function across a kexec

The i2c/spi shutdown hook switches the RK809/RK817 sleep pin to its
power-down function so that the PSCI SYSTEM_OFF that follows a normal
shutdown powers the board down.  kernel_kexec() runs the same
device_shutdown(), but no power-off follows: the next kernel starts with
the pin on its power-down function and nothing restores it (only a
suspend/resume cycle does).  From then on any SoC reset that asserts the
sleep pin turns into a power-off.

On a PineNote (RK3566 + RK817) with the DesignWare watchdog armed just
before kexec -e: SYS_CFG3 reads 0x20 (SLPPIN_NULL_FUN) after a cold boot
and 0x30 (SLPPIN_DN_FUN) after a kexec; when the watchdog expires in the
kexec'd kernel the chip reboots at 0x20 and powers off at 0x30.  A trial
kernel that hangs during boot therefore needs a power button instead of
recovering by watchdog.  Skip the switch while a kexec is in progress.

wilkbook: doc/upstream-register.md item 25; doc/status.md 2026-09-03.

--- a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c	2026-09-03 14:15:37.025994261 -0600
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c	2026-09-03 14:16:22.423779972 -0600
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
+#include <linux/kexec.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/rk808.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/core.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
@@ -738,6 +739,19 @@
 	struct rk808 *rk808 = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * A kexec is not a power-off.  The next kernel inherits the PMIC as
+	 * we leave it, and nothing in its boot restores the sleep pin's
+	 * function (only a suspend/resume cycle does); with the pin left on
+	 * its power-down function every later SoC reset -- a watchdog expiry
+	 * in a kernel that hangs during boot, say -- becomes a power-off
+	 * instead of a restart.  Measured on a PineNote (RK3566 + RK817):
+	 * SYS_CFG3 reads 0x20 on a cold boot and 0x30 after a kexec; the
+	 * armed watchdog reboots the chip at 0x20 and powers it off at 0x30.
+	 */
+	if (kexec_in_progress)
+		return;
+
 	switch (rk808->variant) {
 	case RK805_ID:
 		ret = regmap_update_bits(rk808->regmap,
